Here's the completed code for the myBisection function:

```matlab
function [R] = myBisection(f, a, b, tol)
    if f(a) * f(b) > 0
        R = 'condition not met';
        return;
    end

    while (b - a) / 2 > tol
        c = (a + b) / 2;

        if f(c) == 0
            R = c;
            return;
        end

        if f(c) * f(a) < 0
            b = c;
        else
            a = c;
        end
    end

    R = (a + b) / 2;
end
```

This implementation of the bisection method computes the root of the given function f(x) within the given tolerance, tol. If the input interval [a, b] does not satisfy the prerequisite that f(a) * f(b) < 0, the function will return the string 'condition not met'.

